Hi Gaurav.

Note that the FIRMA scores (and expression values, chip effects, etc.) are stored in the exponentiated (base 2) scale.  So, take log2() of them:

> log2(1568)
[1] 10.6

That's much more feasible.

Cheers,
Mark

